A||||20||RiceCooker||You WILL NOT believe this||||2||
Z||000000||RiceCooker||05-09-2001||10:57 AM||||Well, I get my car back from my mechanic and it's running like a dream. My Clutch saga is finally put to rest. For those who have been following, it was quite a long saga.<P>I Don't even turn on my stereo cause my car is loud and mean and i missed it so much.<P>I get home, eat supper clean up, change my license plate - my new one says "GVN2FLY" and i'm just checkin out the car. I lift forward my seat back where my amp USED to be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <BR>MY AMP IS GONE!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Nothing else in my car was touched. My faceplate was detached but my 12 disc changer was there and left alone (not even the magazine was taken)<P>So my mechanics obviously left it out in their yard unlocked. There is no forced entry whatsoever. <P>They no that my car attracts attention, they know i want it in the shop overnight. <P>Now I have to go back there tonight with my receipt and demand some money. Maybe one of them knows that my car was broken into. Actually it wasn't even broken into, the door was opened and they were probably laughing.<P>One of the mechanics made an expensive mistake and I'm NOT paying for it. <P>Oh yeah, It was a Kenwood 4 channell, 200 watt amp. $300.00 but my friend who works at Future shop got it for me for $230.00. So it's not even my name on the receipt - that doesn't help my case.<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000001||Fiero5||05-09-2001||11:18 AM||||That BITES!<BR>I had the same thing happen a few years ago with my Firebird Formula. It died and I had it towed. They left it in the car yard overnight, and tons of stuff got stolen. My T-Top bags, my stereo, sub woofer and amp, and on and on.<BR>I fought with them for a week till they broke. I threatened to send a letter to the editor or have the newspaper do a story on it, etc. Usually the last thing places like these want, is bad publicity like that. Just scared them enough to take care of it.<P>Steve||||reg||8
Z||000002||Jay||05-09-2001||11:28 AM||||That sucks!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||05-09-2001||11:29 AM||||Sheesh your having a rough time there man. Got all kinds of bad mojo going on.||||reg||4
Z||000004||RiceCooker||05-09-2001||11:39 AM||||Bad Karma<P>I'm feeling mixed emotions<P>I have my car, and it's finally running awesome.<P>It seems like one thing hits after the other. I'm scared to get another amp and put it in. Cause my engine might blow up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Disappointed,<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||05-09-2001||12:18 PM||||That same thing happened to me last summer.  I had my coupe at the shop with 2 subs, an amp, and a nice head unit. about a week after the car had been there, they called me and told me it had all been stolen.<P>we decide they will do all my repairs (needed a lot) for free in payment of the stolen stuff.<P>my car sits there for a month and a half, way longer than the week expected. i finally pick it up and re-buy my stereo.  <P>a few weeks later i take my car to another mechanic to get a balljoint fixed... they tell me a whole bunch of stuff needs to be fixed. i look over the list, agreeing with things like brakes and front suspension, until I get down to things like motor mounts  and bearing- the things this previous guy was supposed to fix. <P>anyway i paid the original guy $200 for a clutch, which he fixed. then he was supposedly going to do some work equalling around $1,000. Damn am I naive.<P>So I sued him in November. Still trying to get the money- $2,050.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||elfiero||05-09-2001||01:00 PM||||Lisa-the mantra I live by;expect to be<BR>screwed by everyone you deal with and that<BR>way if by some slim chance your not,you can<BR>be pleasantly surprised!||||reg||6
Z||000007||Ken Wittlief||05-09-2001||01:24 PM||||Mixed emotions: Watching your mother in law drive off a cliff in your Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000008||V8Fiero||05-09-2001||01:29 PM||||Those stories are the ones why I NEVER take my car to a mechanic!!!!<P><BR>If I dont know how to do something....guess what? Im gonnna learn...hehe<P>Scitt||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||05-09-2001||01:36 PM||||LisaFiero:<P>  noticed on your web site that you are really into restoring and showing Fieros. You need to get connected with some other Fiero-heads in your area that can do things like bushings and serious mechanical work, so you dont have to take your machines to a shop and pay mechanics to do this kinda stuff.<P><BR>  Mechanics and repair shops are for newer cars and for people that dont know any gearheads. If you are gonna be restoring cars this old you really dont want to be paying someone $65+/hr to be doing your 'hobbie' for you.<P>  I mean, if you think about it, thats like hiring some army guy to go out and shoot a deer for you, cause you like hunting.<P>  Check around the web ring - see if there is a Fiero club in your area, or an auto/mechanics club where you are going to school.<P>  I cant think of a better way to spend time than restoring a fine piece of machinery. Just wish I could find a way to get my hands clean at the end of the day. starting to think I should wear gloves or something. might reduce the cuts and punctures I seem to be suffering alot on my fingers too (my fiero keeps biting me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroLisa||05-09-2001||01:55 PM||||Ken,<P>Well I taken my Fiero to a mechanic only once since that incident- to get a water pump in my new GT because I was new in the area and didn't know where I could work on the car except my dorm parking lot. When I took my old coupe to that second shop for the ball joint it was because I had tried to do it in my driveway and didn't have the right tools since that sucker didn't want to come loose.<P>I have learned that mechanics aren't worth my time and money, so I've invested my time into learning as much as I can- and for the most part its been fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||KRMFiero||05-09-2001||02:49 PM||||If there isnt a sign in visable sight that says they are not responsible for theft then you might be able you get a new amp, hopefully anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Taijiguy||05-09-2001||03:06 PM||||I hate to say it, but I think many shops employ people who are inherently dishonest. I never take my car to shop unless I'm on the road and it's an emergency. And then, I'm there babysitting it every step of the way. Within 10 minutes they know I'm street smart and car savvy, and that I'll pick up on any BS they try to hand me.<BR>My sister was ripped off by the same place a dozen times and never knew it until I got involved one time. <BR>She has a Mazda 626, and it started making a horrible squealing noise on Christmas day. I checked it out but had no tools, but I could tell it was the transmission. My guess was it was just very low on fluid. She had AAA so we just had it towed to this place she trusted. They called her the next day and told her it was the clutch and throwout bearing. I knew this was a crock because if you pressed the clutch in, the noise would take a second to stop, as the transmission spun down. I got on the phone, and told them they were full of it, and not to touch the car, I'd come get it. I went over there to pick it up, and while I was there, checked the fluid. Sure enough it was almost empty. I put fuid in it right there in their lot, and brough them out to show them. They argued that it was just temporary, and proceeded to charge my sister 25 bucks for the priveledge of loking at it. I told them we weren't paying and that I'd get the sherriff out there if I had to. (My sister was right there and witnessed everything) They let us go without paying, but we put the word out in every way possible that they were a ripoff.<BR>So if you're in Columbus, avoid the Shell station at the corner of 5th and High. They're ripoffs!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||FLASHY||05-09-2001||03:11 PM||||Awwww MAN!!! Sorry to hear that Todd. I know how you feel. I used to have a '76 VW Beetle with 2 12" Subs, 2 high-end 6x9"s, and a 600 Watt Amp all stolen in my driveway at night. I was mighty ticked off. I "WAS" happy that they didn't damage the car to get in though...until it got broken into again a month later (same driveway at night again) only this time they shattered the window to get in and there was nothing left to steal...freakin' morons I tell you. So we ended up getting video surveillance and of course it never happened again. I had a baseball bat sitting right at my bedroom door waiting for the motion sensor alarm to go off.<P>Anyway, back to fiero talk. I also had my fiero broken into one evening near the Stampede grounds. When I got back to my car I see my passenger window smashed, the seat pushed forward and my CD's stolen. To my surprise, my subs, amp, bass booster, and CD faceplate were all still there! The only thing they took was 6 CD's..can you believe that? I almost would have felt better about it if they stole more stuff...ok maybe not...but it cost me over $200 in repairs over a couple of old CD's. Of course NOW that my insurance covers everything nothing happens anymore. What's up with that anyway?!<P>I guess what I'm trying to say is I hear ya man...and everyone else who's had something stolen or vandalized. It sucks!<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||05-09-2001||03:14 PM||||One surefire way to get ripped off is to let your inspection sticker expire. Here in NY you wont get a ticket if its up to a month overdue<P>BUT<P>when you take a car to be inspected with an overdue sticker, they take it off the car first, then they inspect it.<P>so if anything is wrong, you cant drive it home and fix it yourself, and no you cant work on it in their parking lot, so you are screwed.<P>I took my 2000 Saturn to a Firestone place to get it inspected a few days after the sticker ran out - 1 year old car - 18,000 miles - simple formality, right.<P> Ohhhhh weeellllllll,,, your headlites are out of alignment, $25!!!<P>  I was so pissed, if I had a baseball bat...<P>   But i payed it, and consider it a $25 education - never again!<P>  BTW my headlites point up in the trees now!||||reg||1
Z||000015||Voytek||05-09-2001||04:15 PM||||Flashy: just what were you doing with that baseball bat at night up in your bedroom anyways?||||reg||12
Z||000016||RiceCooker||05-09-2001||04:36 PM||||Voytek, you are twisted<P>Everyone else, thanks for the moral support. It good that the car wasnt smashed or anything cause they didn't actually have to BREAK in. But at the same time, If the car was locked, and or alarmed, they wouldn't have done anything. It was just too easy. <P>Slight, slight possibility is that one of the mechanics that works there decided to take it because he really doesn't like me. I would not accuse him of it but i do not believe this is my financial responsibilty. That being said, that doesn't mean Deerfoot Auto Centre will agree with me.||||reg||6
